{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-616", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/616", "wordCount": 2592, "segments": [{"start": 6.0, "text": "Hello, my name is James"}, {"start": 8.0, "text": "Kelly, and I'm a Software"}, {"start": 9.0, "text": "Engineer on the Game"}, {"start": 10.0, "text": "Technologies Team at Apple."}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "In this video, we'll be talking"}, {"start": 14.0, "text": "about the new features and"}, {"start": 15.0, "text": "changes coming to the Game"}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "Controller framework this year"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "to help you adopt newly"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "supported game controllers."}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "The Game Controller framework"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "has been making it easy to add"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "support for MFi Game Controllers"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "to your games on iOS, tvOS, and"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "macOS."}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "By abstracting controller"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "hardware through a common API,"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "the Game Controller framework"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "lets you write your code once"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "without you having to worry"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "about how controller data is"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "mapped."}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "And this year, we're excited to"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "announce new support for some"}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "fantastic controllers."}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "First is the Bluetooth-enabled"}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "Xbox Wireless controller from"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "Microsoft."}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "This will now seamlessly"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "integrate into any Game"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "Controller framework-enabled"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "game."}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "And that's not all."}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "The DualShock 4 Controller from"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "Sony is now supported by the"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "Game Controller framework."}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "It will just work with any games"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "that already have controller"}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "support through the Game"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "Controller framework."}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "Many developers have already"}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "been creating some great games"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "with controller support."}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "Rayman Adventures, Transistor,"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "Sky Force Reloaded, and Alto's"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "Adventure are some great"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "examples, and just a few of the"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "games on the App Store that"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "support controllers."}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "By using the Game Controller"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "framework, games will"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "automatically support the Xbox"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "Wireless and DualShock 4"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "Controllers in iOS 13, tvOS 13,"}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "and macOS Catalina."}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "In this video, we'll talk about"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "how to grab a reference to these"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "new controllers through the Game"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "Controller framework, how to"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "access their inputs, some UI"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "best practices for probably"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "supporting MFi, Xbox Wireless,"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "and DualShock 4 Controllers, and"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "our recommendations for how to"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "update your games on macOS, if"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "they previously supported Game"}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "Controllers through lower level"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "frameworks such as IOKit."}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "First, let's talk about changes"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "coming to the Game Controller"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "framework in support of these"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "new controllers."}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "As a quick reminder, games that"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "already use the Game Controller"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "framework will gain support for"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "free, meaning if your game"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "supports MFi controllers, it"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "will also automatically support"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "the Xbox Wireless controller and"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "the DualShock 4."}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "The controller's inputs can be"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "accessed via a GCController's"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "GCExtendedGamepad profile."}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "For those of you who are new to"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "the Game Controller framework,"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "let's talk briefly about how to"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "detect a controller."}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "Each controller is represented"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "by a class named GCController."}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "It's the same class for all"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "controllers, MFi, Xbox Wireless,"}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "and DualShock 4 controllers, as"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "well as the serial remote, are"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "all instances of GCController."}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "The first thing you want to do"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "is get a list of currently"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "connected controllers."}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "To do this, use GCController's"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "controllers class method."}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "It returns an array of"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "GCController instances"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "representing all connected"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "controllers."}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "The array will be empty if no"}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "controllers are connected."}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "You should check this array when"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "your app launches and set up the"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "controllers as appropriate."}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "Now it's common for controllers"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "to connect and disconnect while"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "your app is running."}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "For example, the player may turn"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "on their controller after"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "launching your game, their"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "controller may run out of"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "batteries, or they may just take"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "the controller out of range."}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "To be notified of these events,"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "add observers for GCController"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "did connect notification and"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "GCController did disconnect"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "notification."}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "Your application did finish"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "launching with options method is"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "a great place to do this."}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "So, now that you've grabbed onto"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "an instance of a connected"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "controller, let's talk about the"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "buttons and other inputs it may"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "have and how to access them."}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "First, let's recap what inputs"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "are available on a controller."}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "There are two triggers, a"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "directional pad, two"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "thumbsticks, a menu button, four"}, {"start": 248.0, "text": "face buttons, a programmable"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "4-LED strip, and two shoulder"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "buttons."}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "Let's take a closer look at how"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "physical buttons map to the API"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "using the four face buttons as"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "an example."}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "Here we can see a table listing"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "the four face button properties"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "found on a controller's extended"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "gamepad profile."}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "The face buttons of MFi"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "controllers map directly to this"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "API as do the face buttons of an"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "Xbox Wireless controller."}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "Note that there is some subtlety"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "to consider with DualShock 4"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "controllers as they use symbols"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "instead of letters to represent"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "their face buttons."}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "In cases where there may be"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "ambiguity when mapping an input"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "to API, we use the notion of"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "positional equivalents to"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "resolve these mappings."}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "For example, if we consider the"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "face buttons to be four buttons"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "arranged in a diamond on the"}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "right side of a controller, then"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "the bottom cross button is"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "positionally equivalent to the"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "bottom A button of an MFi"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "controller."}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "So, it maps to the button A"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "property."}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "The right face button with a"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "circle button maps to the button"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "B property and so on."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "Next, let's talk about clickable"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "thumbsticks or L3 and R3."}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "We added support for these"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "inputs to the Game Controller"}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "framework in iOS 12.1, tvOS"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "12.1, and macOS Mojave 10.14.1."}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "While the Xbox Wireless and"}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "DualShock 4 controllers all have"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "clickable thumbsticks,"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "thumbsticks on some models of"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "MFi controllers may not be"}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "clickable."}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "Let's dive into a code example"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "to see how we can handle this."}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "Let's say we want to make the"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "player character crouch when the"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "player clicks L3."}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "If we're supporting older"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "versions of iOS, tvOS, or macOS,"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "we should first check to see if"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "we have the clickable"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "thumbsticks API available to us."}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "Even if we do though, the"}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "specific controller we're"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "mapping may not physically have"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "clickable thumbsticks."}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "So, we check to see if the left"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "thumbstick button is new."}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "And if it is, we should ensure"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "that the user interaction we"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "were intending to map to L3, in"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "this case, crouching the player,"}, {"start": 386.0, "text": "is available through some other"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "means."}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "Once we are working with a"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "controller that we know has"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "clickable thumbsticks, we can"}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "just assign our behavior to the"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "press handler of L3."}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "Now, when a player clicks the"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "left thumbstick button, the game"}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "will toggle the player"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "character's crouch."}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "If our game is running on"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "versions of iOS, tvOS, or macOS"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "that don't have this API, we"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "still need to code an alternative path to the player"}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "crouch."}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "Next, let's talk about some new"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "buttons that have been added to"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "the API in support of the Xbox"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "wireless and DualShock 4"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "Controllers, what we're calling"}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "the auxiliary buttons."}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "These buttons are typically"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "found in the middle of"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "controllers."}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "First, we have the menu button."}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "It should be used to pause"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "gameplay and bring up the"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "in-game pause menu."}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "All supported controllers have"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "this button."}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "Now let's look at the options"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "button."}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "It's a general purpose button,"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "but you should avoid using it"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "for time critical actions, as"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "it's generally positioned out of"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "the way."}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "Note that not all controllers"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "have this button."}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "Let's take a look at how these"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "new APIs map to existing MFi"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "controllers."}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "The center menu button maps"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "directly to the button menu"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "property of GCExtendedGamepad."}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "Note that in this example, this"}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "MFi controller doesn't have an"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "options button."}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "So, the button options property"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "of GCExtendedGamepad is new."}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "Next up is the Xbox Wireless"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "controller. When a controller has multiple"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "auxiliary buttons, we determine"}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "its button mapping using"}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "positional equivalents."}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "The right auxiliary button, in"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "this case, the Xbox Wireless"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "controller's menu button maps"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "directly to the button menu"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "property, whereas the left"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "Auxiliary button or the Xbox"}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "Wireless controller's view"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "button maps to the button"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "options property."}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "The Xbox button in the center of"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "the controller has been reserved"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "for system use."}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "The same approach can be applied"}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "for the DualShock 4."}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "Again, we can use positional"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "equivalents to determine the"}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "button mappings."}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "The right auxiliary button or"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "the DualShock 4's options button"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "maps to the button menu"}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "property, whereas the left"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "auxiliary button, the DualShock"}, {"start": 531.0, "text": "4's share button maps to the"}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "button options property."}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "The PS button in the center of"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "the controller has also been"}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "reserved."}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "Note that we've deprecated the"}, {"start": 544.0, "text": "controller paused handler."}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "You should now use the new"}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "button menu API instead."}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "Let's dive into a code example"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "to see how we can handle this."}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "Let's say we want to pause or"}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "unpause the game whenever the"}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "player presses the menu button."}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "If we're supporting older"}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "versions of iOS, tvOS or macOS,"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "we should first check to see if"}, {"start": 567.0, "text": "we have the new menu button API."}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "If we do, we simply register a"}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "pressed changed handler on the"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "extended gamepad's button menu"}, {"start": 576.0, "text": "property."}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "Within the handler, we toggle"}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "the pause menu."}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "Typically, when players want to"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "pause the game, they want to do"}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "it as fast as possible, so we"}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "make sure to trigger this behavior on button press rather"}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "than button release."}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "If the new API isn't available,"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "we should still register our"}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "functionality with the old"}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "controller PausedHandler."}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "This will trigger whenever the"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "menu button is pressed."}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "So that was the menu button."}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "Now let's look at the options"}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "button."}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "Again, remember that not all"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "controllers may have this"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "button."}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "Let's dive into another code"}, {"start": 614.0, "text": "example to see how we should"}, {"start": 616.0, "text": "handle this."}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "Here, we want to bring up an"}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "in-game settings menu whenever"}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "the player presses the options"}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "button."}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "If we're supporting older"}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "versions of iOS, tvOS, or macOS,"}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "we should first check to see if"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "we have the new options button."}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "But even if we do, the"}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "controller we're mapping may not"}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "physically have an options"}, {"start": 637.0, "text": "button."}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "So we check to see if the"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "options button is new."}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "And if it is, we need to ensure"}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "that the settings menu is"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "accessible via some other means."}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "For example, we can list it as"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "an item in the pause menu."}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "If the controller has an options"}, {"start": 653.0, "text": "button, we can just assign our"}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "behavior to the button options"}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "pressed handler."}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "Now, when a player clicks the"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "options button, the game will"}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "toggle the settings menu."}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "If the new API isn't available,"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "we still need to make sure"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "there's an alternative path to"}, {"start": 668.0, "text": "reach the settings menu."}, {"start": 670.0, "text": "So that was a quick look at the"}, {"start": 672.0, "text": "new API coming to the Game"}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "Controller framework this year"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "in support of the newly added"}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "Xbox Wireless and DualShock 4"}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "controllers."}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "Now, let's talk about some UI"}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "best practices for handling"}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "different controllers so that"}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "your users can experience your"}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "game in the best possible way."}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "With the Game Controller"}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "framework being expanded to"}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "support more than just MFi"}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "controllers, a new consideration"}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "arises."}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "Buttons and other inputs may no"}, {"start": 698.0, "text": "longer be visually consistent"}, {"start": 700.0, "text": "between controllers."}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "In this example, the B button in"}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "the prompt only matches the MFi"}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "controller while the Xbox"}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "Wireless controller's B button"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "is red and the DualShock 4 has a"}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "circle button instead."}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "Let's dive deeper into this"}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "example to see how we could"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "handle this."}, {"start": 717.0, "text": "Let's say you're introducing"}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "your player to the base"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "mechanics of your game and you"}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "want to display an in-game"}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "prompt that tells them how to"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "block."}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "In this case, your block"}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "function is mapped to the button"}, {"start": 727.0, "text": "B property of GCExtendedGamepad."}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "For an MFi controller, we"}, {"start": 733.0, "text": "display our MFi B button asset"}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "as we did before."}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "For the Xbox Wireless"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "controller, however, we need to"}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "slightly tweak the asset, in"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "this case, by making the B"}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "button red."}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "Finally, we display a circle"}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "button when the DualShock 4 is"}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "the active controller."}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "Now, regardless of what"}, {"start": 751.0, "text": "controller the player is using,"}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "they can easily understand your"}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "in-game prompts."}, {"start": 755.0, "text": "Let's take a look at a code"}, {"start": 756.0, "text": "example to see how we can"}, {"start": 757.0, "text": "achieve this."}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "Here, we have a simple function"}, {"start": 762.0, "text": "called getBlockButtonAsset that"}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "returns the appropriate art"}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "asset for the block button."}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "First, we switch over the"}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "controller's product category, a"}, {"start": 773.0, "text": "new property added this year to"}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "GCController to determine what"}, {"start": 776.0, "text": "kind of controller it is."}, {"start": 777.0, "text": "If it's an Xbox Wireless"}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "controller, we will return the"}, {"start": 781.0, "text": "red B button asset."}, {"start": 783.0, "text": "If it's a DualShock 4"}, {"start": 785.0, "text": "controller, we'll return the red"}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "circle button asset."}, {"start": 789.0, "text": "And finally, by default,"}, {"start": 791.0, "text": "overturn the MFi green B button"}, {"start": 793.0, "text": "asset."}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "This way, your game will support"}, {"start": 796.0, "text": "the diverse range of MFi"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "controllers currently available"}, {"start": 799.0, "text": "and gracefully fall back to a"}, {"start": 800.0, "text": "sensible asset should new"}, {"start": 801.0, "text": "controller support be added in"}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "the future."}, {"start": 804.0, "text": "Let's return to our previous"}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "block example."}, {"start": 807.0, "text": "Instead of creating unique art"}, {"start": 808.0, "text": "assets for each type of"}, {"start": 809.0, "text": "controller, another option is to"}, {"start": 811.0, "text": "use generic symbols in your"}, {"start": 812.0, "text": "in-game tutorials and prompts."}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "By providing a generic prompt"}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "that doesn't rely on anything"}, {"start": 819.0, "text": "other than positional equivalents, you can rest"}, {"start": 821.0, "text": "assured knowing that your"}, {"start": 822.0, "text": "players will be able to easily"}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "understand your in-game guidance"}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "regardless of what type of"}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "controller is connected."}, {"start": 828.0, "text": "In this example, it's clear that"}, {"start": 830.0, "text": "the players should press the"}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "right face button."}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "One last note, players may have"}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "multiple controllers connected"}, {"start": 838.0, "text": "to their device at the same time"}, {"start": 840.0, "text": "even if they're playing alone."}, {"start": 842.0, "text": "You should gracefully support"}, {"start": 843.0, "text": "all connected controllers in"}, {"start": 844.0, "text": "this case, as a player may"}, {"start": 846.0, "text": "switch between them at any"}, {"start": 847.0, "text": "moment."}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "This means that you'll need to"}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "recognize input from all"}, {"start": 850.0, "text": "connected controllers either by"}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "pulling them each frame or"}, {"start": 854.0, "text": "registering input handlers with"}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "each of them."}, {"start": 857.0, "text": "You should also update your"}, {"start": 858.0, "text": "in-game guidance and visuals to"}, {"start": 860.0, "text": "match the most recently used"}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "controllers."}, {"start": 862.0, "text": "For example, if a player is"}, {"start": 865.0, "text": "using their MFi controller,"}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "display the appropriate MFi art"}, {"start": 868.0, "text": "assets."}, {"start": 870.0, "text": "But if the player pressed an"}, {"start": 872.0, "text": "input on their connected"}, {"start": 873.0, "text": "DualShock 4, all in-game visuals"}, {"start": 875.0, "text": "should automatically adjust to"}, {"start": 877.0, "text": "use the DualShock 4 art assets."}, {"start": 880.0, "text": "By dynamically adapting your"}, {"start": 881.0, "text": "visuals to the most recently"}, {"start": 882.0, "text": "used controller, you will"}, {"start": 883.0, "text": "provide your players an"}, {"start": 885.0, "text": "intuitive and polished"}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "controller-driven experience."}, {"start": 889.0, "text": "Now, for those of you who have"}, {"start": 890.0, "text": "previously implemented the game"}, {"start": 892.0, "text": "controller support outside of"}, {"start": 893.0, "text": "the Game Controller framework on"}, {"start": 894.0, "text": "macOS, we have some new guidance"}, {"start": 896.0, "text": "for your games."}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "When you adopt the Game"}, {"start": 899.0, "text": "Controller framework, game"}, {"start": 901.0, "text": "controllers will just work, so"}, {"start": 902.0, "text": "you should use it for MFi, Xbox"}, {"start": 905.0, "text": "Wireless, and DualShock 4"}, {"start": 906.0, "text": "controller support on macOS."}, {"start": 908.0, "text": "As we abstract away any hardware"}, {"start": 910.0, "text": "intricacies that may differ"}, {"start": 911.0, "text": "between controllers, we provide"}, {"start": 913.0, "text": "you consistency in your app"}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "across iOS, tvOS, and macOS."}, {"start": 918.0, "text": "This will also help to ensure"}, {"start": 920.0, "text": "that your apps remain compatible"}, {"start": 921.0, "text": "with current and future OS"}, {"start": 923.0, "text": "updates."}, {"start": 924.0, "text": "For those of you who have"}, {"start": 926.0, "text": "previously hardcoded support for"}, {"start": 928.0, "text": "these controllers through lower"}, {"start": 929.0, "text": "level APIs such as IOKit, we"}, {"start": 931.0, "text": "highly recommend that you move"}, {"start": 933.0, "text": "your implementation over to the"}, {"start": 934.0, "text": "Game Controller framework."}, {"start": 936.0, "text": "As new controllers will appear"}, {"start": 938.0, "text": "in both IOKit and the Game"}, {"start": 939.0, "text": "Controller framework, you should"}, {"start": 941.0, "text": "drop your IOKit implementation"}, {"start": 942.0, "text": "to ensure there are no"}, {"start": 943.0, "text": "conflicts."}, {"start": 945.0, "text": "This will allow you to code to a"}, {"start": 946.0, "text": "single interface and receive new"}, {"start": 948.0, "text": "game controller support for"}, {"start": 949.0, "text": "free."}, {"start": 953.0, "text": "So let's summarize what we've"}, {"start": 955.0, "text": "discussed in this video."}, {"start": 957.0, "text": "The Game Controller framework"}, {"start": 959.0, "text": "abstracts hardware through a"}, {"start": 960.0, "text": "common API, letting you write"}, {"start": 961.0, "text": "your code once without having to"}, {"start": 963.0, "text": "worry about the low-level"}, {"start": 964.0, "text": "differences between controller"}, {"start": 965.0, "text": "models."}, {"start": 967.0, "text": "This has the great benefit of"}, {"start": 968.0, "text": "allowing your game to"}, {"start": 969.0, "text": "automatically support newly"}, {"start": 970.0, "text": "added controllers such as the"}, {"start": 972.0, "text": "Xbox Wireless and the DualShock"}, {"start": 973.0, "text": "4 controllers."}, {"start": 975.0, "text": "However, in order to provide the"}, {"start": 977.0, "text": "best user experience for your"}, {"start": 978.0, "text": "players, you should take care to"}, {"start": 980.0, "text": "adapt your game's UI and"}, {"start": 982.0, "text": "on-screen indicators to the"}, {"start": 983.0, "text": "active controller."}, {"start": 985.0, "text": "And finally, ensure your macOS"}, {"start": 987.0, "text": "apps stay compatible with future"}, {"start": 989.0, "text": "OS updates by migrating existing"}, {"start": 991.0, "text": "controller support from lower"}, {"start": 992.0, "text": "level APIs to the Game"}, {"start": 993.0, "text": "Controller framework."}, {"start": 995.0, "text": "More information about this"}, {"start": 997.0, "text": "year's game controller update"}, {"start": 998.0, "text": "can be found on the Apple"}, {"start": 999.0, "text": "developer site."}, {"start": 1003.0, "text": "That's it for this year's game"}, {"start": 1004.0, "text": "controller's update."}, {"start": 1005.0, "text": "Thank you for watching."}, {"start": 1006.0, "text": "We hope you found this"}, {"start": 1007.0, "text": "information helpful and you can"}, {"start": 1009.0, "text": "use it to create some awesome"}, {"start": 1010.0, "text": "games with game controller"}]}
